  "notes": "Quarter-by-quarter Program of Study from Appendix A of Galen's official 'Application for Intent to Open a Physical Building and Establish a Nursing Education Program: Baccalaureate Degree in Nursing Program' submitted to the Utah Board of Nursing (October 6, 2022) for the Salt Lake Campus, 344 West 13800 South, Draper, UT 84020. The filing states the BSN 'is currently offered at other Galen campuses, has an existing faculty-developed curriculum' (CCNE-accredited at those locations). Galen announced the 3-Year BSN launched at the Salt Lake City campus in September 2026 (first cohort began September 29, 2026). The plan cross-validates with Indiana's official workforce registry listing for Galen's BSN Prelicensure: 36 months, 160 academic credit hours on the quarter calendar. Galen runs on a QUARTER calendar; seeded as published in quarters. Two 4-quarter-credit slots ('Elective Course 1' and 'Elective Course 2') are choice slots. Downstream semester-gated checks (associate 4-7 / bachelor 8-12 semester gates) are semester-calibrated and do not apply to quarter terms without conversion. No course-level prerequisites are listed in the plan of study tables.",
